      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It's specifically the duplicate name check, if you comment it out in the source for the SDK, the issue goes away.\nThe issue is two fold:\nFirst is that this check is expensive, exponentially moreso the larger the world is (down to GameObject count specifically it seems).\nSecond is that this check is ran EVERY TIME YOU FOCUS THE SDK WINDOW. Which means if you click away to do something else while the check is locking up Unity, the moment you click back into Unity, the SDK will run the check again. This can very easily result in what looks like an infinite deadlock if you don't realise what's happening.\nThis check needs to be made optional or a manual trigger. How it currently works is very badly designed and only works as expected on very small projects.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
