  "created": "2021-09-01T04:15:08.020Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I have some pretty massive projects and scenes for maps. The larger they are the longer the window hangs. It seems to be running checks for duplicate names among other things non-stop. Even with there being no problems, I have to click Build & Publish hundreds of times until I get lucky enough for it to not be hung up. Then it will build the project. Is there a way we can either A. Get the checks added to a button we can manually run or B. Get a dropdown on the Tool bar called \"Quick Build\" where if there are no errors it'll just build so going into that menu that's locked up instead needed. Or separate the Builder Tab and \"Error Checks\" into another tab.",
